<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 412)</h2>
<p><b>Aspect guides that know where the picture really is.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>When a preview is an envelope around the true camera image — a 4:3 open gate rendered inside a 16:9 QuickTime — guides can now measure the <b>camera gate</b> instead of the container: Aspect Guides → Measure From, or <b>Auto-Detect Gate</b> (finds the rendered black bars), or automatically from pipelines that stamp <code>camera_gate</code> on the Kitsu shot.</li>
<li>The gate draws as a dashed outline, every guide computes inside it, and the setting saves with the clip.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
